{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788349132870,"sessionID":"ses_f9e164660ffebnFfYprynYTI1L","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_5e37e3e2d9314ea4bb6ec177","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/references/constexpr-guide.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/references/constexpr-guide.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # pyasc ConstExpr Guide\n2: \n3: ## What is ConstExpr?\n4: \n5: `asc.ConstExpr[T]` wraps a parameter type to indicate it must be resolved at compile time, not at runtime. The JIT compiler uses the concrete value to specialize the generated code.\n6: \n7: ## When to use\n8: \n9: 1. **Compile-time branching**: When an `if` condition determines code structure\n10: 2. **Unsupported runtime types**: When you need `str`, `tuple`, `list`, or `dict` as parameters\n11: 3. **Variable scoping**: When a variable is only assigned in one branch of an `if`\n12: \n13: ## Example: Compile-time branching\n14: \n15: ```python\n16: @asc.jit\n17: def kernel(x: asc.GlobalAddress, z: asc.GlobalAddress, mode: asc.ConstExpr[int], n: int):\n18:     offset = asc.get_block_idx() * n\n19:     x_gm = asc.GlobalTensor()\n20:     z_gm = asc.GlobalTensor()\n21:     x_gm.set_global_buffer(x + offset, n)\n22:     z_gm.set_global_buffer(z + offset, n)\n23: \n24:     if mode == 1:\n25:         # This branch is resolved at compile time\n26:         # Only the matching branch is compiled\n27:         ...\n28:     elif mode == 2:\n29:         ...\n30: ```\n31: \n32: ## Example: If-scoped variable fix\n33: \n34: Without ConstExpr (broken):\n35: ```python\n36: @asc.jit\n37: def func(x):           # x is runtime, compiler can't resolve branch\n38:     if x:\n39:         y = 1\n40:     z = y + 2           # ERROR: y may not be defined\n41: ```\n42: \n43: With ConstExpr (fixed):\n44: ```python\n45: @asc.jit\n46: def func(x: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n47:     if x:               # resolved at compile time\n48:         y = 1\n49:     z = y + 2           # OK: compiler knows which branch is taken\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ## Limitations\n53: \n54: - `ConstExpr` parameters become part of the cache key\n55: - Different `ConstExpr` values produce different compiled kernels\n56: - Overuse increases compilation time and cache size\n\n(End of file - total 56 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# pyasc ConstExpr Guide\n\n## What is ConstExpr?\n\n`asc.ConstExpr[T]` wraps a parameter type to indicate it must be resolved at compile time, not at runtime. The JIT compiler uses the concrete value to specialize the generated code.\n\n## When to use\n\n1. **Compile-time branching**: When an `if` condition determines code structure\n2. **Unsupported runtime types**: When you need `str`, `tuple`, `list`, or `dict` as parameters\n3. **Variable scoping**: When a variable is only assigned in one branch of an `if`\n\n## Example: Compile-time branching\n\n```python\n@asc.jit\ndef kernel(x: asc.GlobalAddress, z: asc.GlobalAddress, mode: asc.ConstExpr[int], n: int):\n    offset = asc.get_block_idx() * n\n    x_gm = asc.GlobalTensor()\n    z_gm = asc.GlobalTensor()","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/references/constexpr-guide.md","text":"# pyasc ConstExpr Guide\n\n## What is ConstExpr?\n\n`asc.ConstExpr[T]` wraps a parameter type to indicate it must be resolved at compile time, not at runtime. The JIT compiler uses the concrete value to specialize the generated code.\n\n## When to use\n\n1. **Compile-time branching**: When an `if` condition determines code structure\n2. **Unsupported runtime types**: When you need `str`, `tuple`, `list`, or `dict` as parameters\n3. **Variable scoping**: When a variable is only assigned in one branch of an `if`\n\n## Example: Compile-time branching\n\n```python\n@asc.jit\ndef kernel(x: asc.GlobalAddress, z: asc.GlobalAddress, mode: asc.ConstExpr[int], n: int):\n    offset = asc.get_block_idx() * n\n    x_gm = asc.GlobalTensor()\n    z_gm = asc.GlobalTensor()\n    x_gm.set_global_buffer(x + offset, n)\n    z_gm.set_global_buffer(z + offset, n)\n\n    if mode == 1:\n        # This branch is resolved at compile time\n        # Only the matching branch is compiled\n        ...\n    elif mode == 2:\n        ...\n```\n\n## Example: If-scoped variable fix\n\nWithout ConstExpr (broken):\n```python\n@asc.jit\ndef func(x):           # x is runtime, compiler can't resolve branch\n    if x:\n        y = 1\n    z = y + 2           # ERROR: y may not be defined\n```\n\nWith ConstExpr (fixed):\n```python\n@asc.jit\ndef func(x: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    if x:               # resolved at compile time\n        y = 1\n    z = y + 2           # OK: compiler knows which branch is taken\n```\n\n## Limitations\n\n- `ConstExpr` parameters become part of the cache key\n- Different `ConstExpr` values produce different compiled kernels\n- Overuse increases compilation time and cache size","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":56,"totalLines":56,"truncated":false}},"title":"skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/references/constexpr-guide.md","time":{"start":1788349132864,"end":1788349132869}},"id":"prt_061ea2f1b001U2wDPhRt6DeREy","sessionID":"ses_f9e164660ffebnFfYprynYTI1L","messageID":"msg_061ea14f2001yNbz0X51t10f7z"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788349133303,"sessionID":"ses_f9e164660ffebnFfYprynYTI1L","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_08849f4881324b2ba5102b41","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/references/type-constraints.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/references/type-constraints.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # pyasc Type Constraints\n2: \n3: ## Kernel parameter types\n4: \n5: ### Supported as runtime parameters\n6: \n7: | Type | Description | Example |\n8: |------|-------------|---------|\n9: | `bool` | Boolean | `def kernel(flag: bool)` |\n10: | `int` | Integer | `def kernel(n: int)` |\n11: | `float` | Float | `def kernel(scale: float)` |\n12: | `numpy` scalar | numpy scalar types | `def kernel(val: np.float32)` |\n13: | `numpy.ndarray` | numpy array | Passed as data |\n14: | `torch.Tensor` | PyTorch tensor (NPU mode only) | Auto H2D/D2H transfer |\n15: | `asc.GlobalAddress` | Global memory pointer | Explicit memory management |\n16: \n17: ### Not supported as runtime parameters\n18: \n19: | Type | Workaround |\n20: |------|------------|\n21: | `str` | Use `asc.ConstExpr[str]` for compile-time strings |\n22: | `tuple` | Use `asc.ConstExpr[tuple]` or pass elements separately |\n23: | `list` | Use `asc.ConstExpr[list]` or pass elements separately |\n24: | `dict` | Use `asc.ConstExpr[dict]` or decompose |\n25: | Complex objects | Decompose into supported scalar/tensor types |\n26: \n27: ## Compile-time parameters (ConstExpr)\n28: \n29: For values resolved at compile time:\n30: \n31: ```python\n32: @asc.jit\n33: def kernel(x: asc.GlobalAddress, mode: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n34:     if mode == 1:    # resolved at compile time, not runtime\n35:         ...\n36:     elif mode == 2:\n37:         ...\n38: ```\n39: \n40: `ConstExpr` is useful for:\n41: - Branch selection that should be resolved at compile time\n42: - Container parameters (tuple, list, dict)\n43: - String parameters\n44: - Any value that changes the compiled code structure\n45: \n46: ## Built-in whitelist\n47: \n48: Only these built-in functions are available inside `@asc.jit`:\n49: \n50: | Built-in | Available |\n51: |----------|-----------|\n52: | `dict` | Yes |\n53: | `float` | Yes |\n54: | `int` | Yes |\n55: | `isinstance` | Yes |\n56: | `issubclass` | Yes |\n57: | `len` | Yes |\n58: | `list` | Yes |\n59: | `range` | Yes |\n60: | `repr` | Yes |\n61: | `str` | Yes |\n62: | `tuple` | Yes |\n63: | `type` | Yes |\n64: | `print` | **No** |\n65: | `open` | **No** |\n66: | `input` | **No** |\n67: | `map`, `filter`, `zip` | **No** |\n68: | `sorted`, `reversed` | **No** |\n69: | Any stdlib | **No** |\n70: \n71: ## Tensor dtype\n72: \n73: Tensor data types are accessed from the tensor itself:\n74: \n75: ```python\n76: data_type = x.dtype           # from GlobalAddress parameter\n77: buffer_size = n * data_type.sizeof()\n78: ```\n79: \n80: Common dtypes: `asc.float32`, `asc.float16`, `asc.int32`, `asc.int8`\n\n(End of file - total 80 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# pyasc Type Constraints\n\n## Kernel parameter types\n\n### Supported as runtime parameters\n\n| Type | Description | Example |\n|------|-------------|---------|\n| `bool` | Boolean | `def kernel(flag: bool)` |\n| `int` | Integer | `def kernel(n: int)` |\n| `float` | Float | `def kernel(scale: float)` |\n| `numpy` scalar | numpy scalar types | `def kernel(val: np.float32)` |\n| `numpy.ndarray` | numpy array | Passed as data |\n| `torch.Tensor` | PyTorch tensor (NPU mode only) | Auto H2D/D2H transfer |\n| `asc.GlobalAddress` | Global memory pointer | Explicit memory management |\n\n### Not supported as runtime parameters\n\n| Type | Workaround |\n|------|------------|","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/references/type-constraints.md","text":"# pyasc Type Constraints\n\n## Kernel parameter types\n\n### Supported as runtime parameters\n\n| Type | Description | Example |\n|------|-------------|---------|\n| `bool` | Boolean | `def kernel(flag: bool)` |\n| `int` | Integer | `def kernel(n: int)` |\n| `float` | Float | `def kernel(scale: float)` |\n| `numpy` scalar | numpy scalar types | `def kernel(val: np.float32)` |\n| `numpy.ndarray` | numpy array | Passed as data |\n| `torch.Tensor` | PyTorch tensor (NPU mode only) | Auto H2D/D2H transfer |\n| `asc.GlobalAddress` | Global memory pointer | Explicit memory management |\n\n### Not supported as runtime parameters\n\n| Type | Workaround |\n|------|------------|\n| `str` | Use `asc.ConstExpr[str]` for compile-time strings |\n| `tuple` | Use `asc.ConstExpr[tuple]` or pass elements separately |\n| `list` | Use `asc.ConstExpr[list]` or pass elements separately |\n| `dict` | Use `asc.ConstExpr[dict]` or decompose |\n| Complex objects | Decompose into supported scalar/tensor types |\n\n## Compile-time parameters (ConstExpr)\n\nFor values resolved at compile time:\n\n```python\n@asc.jit\ndef kernel(x: asc.GlobalAddress, mode: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    if mode == 1:    # resolved at compile time, not runtime\n        ...\n    elif mode == 2:\n        ...\n```\n\n`ConstExpr` is useful for:\n- Branch selection that should be resolved at compile time\n- Container parameters (tuple, list, dict)\n- String parameters\n- Any value that changes the compiled code structure\n\n## Built-in whitelist\n\nOnly these built-in functions are available inside `@asc.jit`:\n\n| Built-in | Available |\n|----------|-----------|\n| `dict` | Yes |\n| `float` | Yes |\n| `int` | Yes |\n| `isinstance` | Yes |\n| `issubclass` | Yes |\n| `len` | Yes |\n| `list` | Yes |\n| `range` | Yes |\n| `repr` | Yes |\n| `str` | Yes |\n| `tuple` | Yes |\n| `type` | Yes |\n| `print` | **No** |\n| `open` | **No** |\n| `input` | **No** |\n| `map`, `filter`, `zip` | **No** |\n| `sorted`, `reversed` | **No** |\n| Any stdlib | **No** |\n\n## Tensor dtype\n\nTensor data types are accessed from the tensor itself:\n\n```python\ndata_type = x.dtype           # from GlobalAddress parameter\nbuffer_size = n * data_type.sizeof()\n```\n\nCommon dtypes: `asc.float32`, `asc.float16`, `asc.int32`, `asc.int8`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":80,"totalLines":80,"truncated":false}},"title":"skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/references/type-constraints.md","time":{"start":1788349133292,"end":1788349133302}},"id":"prt_061ea309400167gsCtcJrU0reJ","sessionID":"ses_f9e164660ffebnFfYprynYTI1L","messageID":"msg_061ea14f2001yNbz0X51t10f7z"}}
